{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.DilogPartBBoundarySeed","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DilogPartBBoundarySeed","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.NegMulLog"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.boundary_term_vanishes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.boundary_term_vanishes","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartBBoundarySeed.lean#L40-L71","doc":"**Conditional boundary-term limit (the \"positive direction\" of the W-P1\nresidual).**  Along any filter `l`, if the endpoint gap `δ` tends to `0⁺` and\nis bounded below by a fixed multiple of the width `w` (`c·w ≤ δ`, `c > 0` —\nthe Diophantine / no-resonance condition), then the boundary term\n`w·(−log δ) → 0`.\n\nApplied with `δ = 1 − xqⁿ`, `w = q − 1`, this closes the W-P1 boundary limit\n`(q−1)·log(1−xqⁿ) → 0` **whenever** `x` satisfies the no-resonance bound\n`1 − xqⁿ ≥ c(q−1)` — the precise hypothesis under which W-P1 converges.\nProof: squeeze `0 ≤ w(−log δ) ≤ (δ/c)(−log δ) = −(1/c)·(δ log δ) → 0` by the\nseed `tendsto_mul_log_nhdsWithin_zero`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.tendsto_mul_log_nhdsWithin_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.tendsto_mul_log_nhdsWithin_zero","kind":"theorem","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartBBoundarySeed.lean#L24-L38","doc":"**Analytic seed — `t·log t → 0` as `t → 0⁺`.**  Immediate from the continuity\nof the entropy function `Real.negMulLog t = −t·log t` at `0`\n(`Real.negMulLog_zero : negMulLog 0 = 0`).  This is the ingredient that\ncontrols the W-P1 boundary term `(q−1)·log(1−xqⁿ)` once the endpoint\n`1−xqⁿ` is bounded below by a multiple of `q−1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}